/-! # The Konyagin–Schlag minimum modulus bound

The first moment bounds the probability of finding a small value by counting
mesh sites near a minimum. The common Fourier estimates use a symmetric
block of independent signs. An optional final sign extends this block to odd
degree. Dropping it gives even degree on the same probability space. At the
two real endpoints the even-degree polynomial is a sum of an odd number of
signs, so its value there has absolute value at least one.

The shared estimates and the odd-degree argument come from the companion
proof at Thomassien/open-math-agents, commit 786f90311bfae6d4107be317e52b5699fcd09663.
The optional final sign and the joint parity conclusion are the adaptation here.

